{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>You are children to YHWH your Elohim.</b> And therefore, if your father of flesh and blood dies, you shall not gash yourselves, for you are not thereby orphaned, since you have a Father who is alive and endures, may His name be blessed and exalted. But the gentiles, when their father dies, must gash themselves, for they no longer have a father but only wood and stone, which are of no avail, as it is written: ״who say to the wood, you are my father, and to the stone, you gave birth to me.״"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:00:55.534974161Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}